// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Cornutus 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1411549164" "Thanks to the intervention of some unscrupulous time travelers, Cornutus the Minotaur managed to kill Theseus and escape his labyrinthine prison on Crete. Constantly on the run from Attican assassins, Cornutus flaunted the laws of both man and the Gods for many years. In his travels, he encountered two beautiful sisters, disciples of Artemis, who mistook him for the avatar of the gods, who often like to take the forms of animals. Cornutus likes the money and the thrill of fighting in the Coliseum and he wields his massive axe with freakish strength and brutality, making him a crowd favorite."
// GroupDescription :
"P627329586" "Time Gladiator"
// DisplayNames :
"P1482639412" "Cornutus the Minotaur"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Cornutus_Finale 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Claudia 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P320635485" "A deadly bow priestess of Artemis, Claudia honors the gods through combat but she has gone restless with the constant demands of the Coliseum. She doesn't really think that Cornutus is blessed by the gods, but doesn't want to say anything for fear that it might upset her more pious sister Camilla. Claudia longs for the day when the gods will grow weary of the constant bloodshed and demand different homage from them but she doesn't expect it any time soon."
// GroupDescription :
"P2364029353" "Handmaidens"
// DisplayNames :
"P2925433652" "Claudia"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Camilla 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3047870135" "A deadly bow priestess of Artemis, Camilla honors the gods with every foe she defeats. She truly believes that Cornutus is divinely blessed and will follow him anywhere as a result. As a testament to their skill with the bow and the staggering amount of enemies they have bested, the gods have rewards the sisters with wings so that they might better commune with the divine."
// DisplayNames :
"P3197837361" "Camilla"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Frank_McCain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2346931434" "A famed card shark and gunslinger from the Wild West, Frank "Hunnerd Yard" McCain was known especially for his tremendous accuracy at great range. Frank McCain's life changed that hot dusty night when he won a strange device from an odd foreign sounding fellow in a game of cards. Figuring it was some kind of new-fangled, steam-powered still, McCain took it back to his shack and fiddled with it. To his amazement, it lit up as bright as the noon-day sun. Next thing he knew, he was lost in the ancient world with nothing but his guns, his dogs and a broken time travel machine. He now lives like an emperor off the prizes he wins in the Coliseum."
// DisplayNames :
"P2210981052" "Frank "Hunnerd Yard" McCain"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Frank_McCain_Finale 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Butch 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P3295087356" "One of Frank McCain's dogs, Butch is a savage yet loyal companion to his gun-toting master."
// GroupDescription :
"P1616818862" "McCain's Maulers"
// DisplayNames :
"P3870407960" "Butch"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Lee 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P4028296924" "One of Frank McCain's dogs, Lee is the youngest and most gentle of the pack.  That doesn't keep him from being able to take down a full-grown man"
// DisplayNames :
"P2744362883" "Lee"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Petey 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1286731150" "One of Frank McCain's dogs, Petey is a savage yet loyal companion to his gun-toting master.  He's also McCain's favorite."
// DisplayNames :
"P2422384913" "Petey"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Killer 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P191666265" "The alpha wolf of Frank McCain's pack of dogs, Killer has a will of his own and doesn't always join McCain in the Coliseum.  When there's a genuine threat to the pack Killer is always there."
// DisplayNames :
"P3603151677" "Killer"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Armageddon 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2611774152" "In the year 2352, a mad scientist designed a powerful doomsday weapon known as the World-Breaker Engine and crafted four robot guardians to harness and channel the destructive energies it created. Armageddon was one such guardian. Fueled by the World-Breaker Engine, Armageddon's powers were near limitless, along with his brethren Apocalypse, Gotterdammerung and Gehenna. So great was their might that they could not be destroyed but were instead cast through time and scattered across the ages. Three of the four have reunited and they bide their time in the Coliseum, waiting to be reunited with their lost brother and the Engine that will fuel the end of the world."
// DisplayNames :
"P3713983168" "Armageddon"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Apocalypse 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P95483744" "In the year 2352, a mad scientist designed a powerful doomsday weapon known as the World-Breaker Engine and crafted four robot guardians to harness and channel the destructive energies it created. Apocalypse was one such guardian. Fueled by the World-Breaker Engine, Apocalypse's powers were near limitless, along with his brethren Armageddon, Gotterdammerung and Gehenna. So great was their might that they could not be destroyed but were instead cast through time and scattered across the ages. Three of the four have reunited and they bide their time in the Coliseum, waiting to be reunited with their lost brother and the Engine that will fuel the end of the world."
// DisplayNames :
"P899833157" "Apocalypse"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Gotterdammerung 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P973486658" "In the year 2352, a mad scientist designed a powerful doomsday weapon known as the World-Breaker Engine and crafted four robot guardians to harness and channel the destructive energies it created. Gotterdammerung was one such guardian. Fueled by the World-Breaker Engine, Gotterdammerung's powers were near limitless, along with his brethren Apocalypse, Armageddon and Gehenna. So great was their might that they could not be destroyed but were instead cast through time and scattered across the ages. Three of the four have reunited and they bide their time in the Coliseum, waiting to be reunited with their lost brother and the Engine that will fuel the end of the world."
// DisplayNames :
"P2079147638" "Gotterdammerung"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_Gotterdammerung_Finale 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Coliseum_God_Champion 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P1897106171" "A hero from the lost-age of Myth, the God-Champion constructed the Coliseum in time immemorial. Brooding like a spider in its web, the God-Champion has feasted on the sweet nectar of violence ever since. For generations, the God-Champion has waited for a challenger worthy of his power and has grown overwhelmingly more powerful with each combatant defeated on the brutal sands. Now that a group of challengers have proven themselves worthy, he takes up sword and shield once more as the souls of the vanquished flock to his side for a chance to bathe once more in the glory of the Coliseum."
// DisplayNames :
"P3260626368" "The God Champion"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Heist_Sylvia_Rexson 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P122721071" "Confidant, assistant, attache and paramour to Ted Dubois, Sylvia Rexson handles many of the day-to-day operations of the Tyrant's Palace Casino. However, you get the feeling that she is capable of far deadlier pursuits."
// GroupDescription :
"P364928701" "Personal Assistant"
// DisplayNames :
"P548785586" "Sylvia Rexson"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Heist_Sylvia_Rexson_Combat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2433389685" "Confidant, assistant, attache and paramour to Ted Dubois, Sylvia Rexson handles many of the day-to-day operations of Tyrant's Palace while also moonlighting as an assassin for hire.  Unlike most casinos that use brute thugs to dissuade thieves and con artists, Sylvia Rexson has used her deadly arts to cultivate a horrible legend regarding what happens to those that attempt to steal, cheat or defraud the casino."
// GroupDescription :
"P4002207004" "Elite Assassin"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Heist_Mr_DuBois 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2512749827" "Chief of Security for Tyrant's Palace, Ted Dubois has run the casino with brutal efficiency for years.  With the help of his assistant, Sylvia Rexson, no one has managed to successfully pull off a job on the Casino on his watch.  Ted Dubois is brutal and completely without sentiment and he maintains a hawk-eyed vigil over his casino, observing everything that occurs with an exacting attention to detail."
// GroupDescription :
"P2440193308" "Tyrant's Palace Security"
// DisplayNames :
"P3750006219" "Mr. DuBois"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Heist_Mr_DuBois_Combat 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Villain Def - SummerEvent_Heist_Jimmy_Crescendo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DisplayDescription :
"P2689216797" "Gambler and crooner, Jimmy Crescendo knows Ted Dubois from their days as military special forces.  Jimmy's experiences overseas changed him and he's had problems returning to civilian life.  Ted Dubois keeps him around the casino for those times when things get a bit dicey, though he's grown increasingly concerned with Jimmy's obsession with demonology and occult.  Ironically, Jimmy has the voice of an angel and keeps the ladies coming around on a nightly basis, but his dark temper and complete lack of humanity make him an ideal strong-arm for the casino."
// GroupDescription :
"P538493078" "Crooner Extraordinaire"
// DisplayNames :
"P2085701227" "Jimmy Crescendo"

